  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "REASONING RELEASE — implements and extends the techniques from \"Build a Reasoning Model (From Scratch)\". VERIFIER: new from-scratch symbolic math verifier (MathVerifier) — \\boxed{} extraction with balanced braces, LaTeX normalization (fractions, surds, degrees, superscripts, mixed numbers, thousands separators), and exact BigInteger-rational equivalence (0.5 = 1/2 exactly, 0.3333333333 != 1/3), perfect-square-aware sqrt, and random-rational-point identity testing for expressions with variables. Grades LaTeX mixed numbers correctly (3\\frac{1}{2} = 7/2) — a case the SymPy reference pipelines get wrong. EVAL: MATH-500 benchmark (fuuga eval --benchmark math500) with per-difficulty-level sub-scores and maj@K self-consistency voting (--maj-k) where answers group by mathematical equivalence, not string equality. RL: rollout scoring is now trajectory-faithful — policy log-probs are computed on the exact sampled token stream (injected ThinkStart, generated ThinkEnd, terminal EOS) via the new generateRollout API, instead of a re-tokenized approximation that dropped control tokens; --thinking samples chain-of-thought rollouts; --reward math scores with the symbolic verifier (\\boxed required); accuracy rewards score ONLY the answer span after think_end, so truncated reasoning can never be rewarded as correct. New GRPO options: DAPO zero-signal group skipping (default ON; --keep-uniform-groups to disable), Dr. GRPO advantage normalization (--no-adv-std), DAPO token-level length-normalized loss that also keeps the KL term length-invariant (--token-level-loss). BEHAVIOR CHANGES: the LR schedule now counts PPO inner iterations (previously it pinned at minimum LR halfway through each epoch), uniform-reward groups are skipped by default, and epoch logs report zero-signal group counts — existing runs will not reproduce bit-identically, deliberately. DATA: fuuga fetch-math-data downloads the 12k MATH training subset (disjoint from MATH-500) as RL JSONL; fuuga sample-traces does rejection-sampling data curation (STaR/RFT): sample N per prompt, keep verifier-passing traces, write SFT JSONL — with --thinking the traces carry tagged reasoning spans. Distillation from R1-style teachers now captures reasoning_content/reasoning and wraps it as think spans by default (--endpoint-no-thinking to drop); fuuga sft --filter-overlong drops over-budget examples instead of truncating away their final answers. INFERENCE: self-consistency voting (fuuga infer --consensus N) and tree-of-thoughts beam search (--tot branch,beam,depth) with verifier-scored states; s1-style thinking budgets (--max-thinking-tokens forces the answer at the cap, --min-thinking-tokens suppresses premature end-of-thinking and injects a Wait, continuation cue) — enforced from the very first sampled token.",
